---
import { site } from '../data/site';
import { defaultLocale } from '../data/i18n';
import SiteHeader from '../components/SiteHeader.astro';
import '../styles/global.css';
import '../styles/directory.css';
---
<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
<head><meta charset="UTF-8"/><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1"/><meta name="robots" content="noindex"/><meta name="description" content={`This ${site.name} page or data file does not exist.`}/><meta name="theme-color" content="#b3450e"/><link rel="icon" href="/favicon.svg" type="image/svg+xml"/><link rel="icon" href="/favicon.ico" sizes="32x32"/><link rel="apple-touch-icon" href="/apple-touch-icon.png"/><title>Page not found · {site.name}</title></head>
<body>
<SiteHeader locale={defaultLocale} path="/"/>
<main class="policy-page">
<p class="eyebrow">404 · NOT FOUND</p>
<h1>That page or data file is not here.</h1>
<p>Protocols and their downloads change between releases. A results file that existed in an earlier release may have been withdrawn, renamed, or replaced after a rights or scientific review — withdrawn evidence is removed rather than left in place, and every hold is recorded in <a href="/releases/#holds">the holds register</a> and every correction in <a href="/releases/#corrections">the corrections register</a>.</p>
<div class="policy-summary"><strong>Looking for a results file?</strong><p>Every protocol currently published has its own page, CSV and protocol JSON, listed at <a href="/protocols/">/protocols/</a>. Every file any release ships is on <a href="/releases/">/releases/</a> with its SHA-256. The combined core export is always at <a href="/data/experiments.json">/data/experiments.json</a>.</p></div>
<section><h2>Where to go next</h2><ul>
<li><a href="/topics/">Questions</a> — every question the evidence can answer, and which kinds of transfer have been measured.</li>
<li><a href="/methods/">Methods</a> — each method's published results, and the model directory: what has been evaluated and what has not.</li>
<li><a href="/datasets/">Datasets</a> — each dataset's results, and the register of sources, terms and attribution.</li>
<li><a href="/releases/#holds">Holds</a> — what is held back, since when, and why; <a href="/releases/#corrections">corrections</a> to released wording.</li>
<li><a href="/data-use/">Data use &amp; privacy</a> — what is published and what stays local.</li>
</ul></section>
</main>
<footer><a class="brand" href="/">{site.name}</a><p>Aggregate results. Credited sources. Research use.</p><a href="/data-use/">Data use &amp; privacy</a><a href="/#overview">Back to results ↑</a></footer>
</body></html>
